Following the discussion in PR [#62074](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/pull/62074), I implemented more useful routing annotations by means of annotation scanning in the class encapsulated based on Symfony Router.All my annotations are implemented relying on middlewares. The Router scans to detect annotations and writes them into attributes.

```php
// 1. Perform reflection scanning
$scannedData = $this->scanForMiddlewareAndAttributes($controller, $method);

// 2. Construct standard attributes
$attributes = array_merge($params, [
    '_controller' => $controller . '::' . $method,
    '_route'      => 'auto_route_' . md5($controller . $method),

    // 🔥 No longer an empty array here, but filled with scanned results
    '_middleware' => $scannedData['middleware'],
    '_auth'       => $scannedData['auth'],
    '_roles'      => $scannedData['roles'],
    '_attributes' => $scannedData['attributesMap'],
]);

$request->attributes->add($attributes);
```

In the middleware dispatcher:
```php
$rawRouteMiddleware = $request->attributes->get('_middleware', []);
        $flattenedRouteMiddleware = $this->flattenArray($rawRouteMiddleware);

            $middlewareChain = function ($req) use ($middleware, $middlewareChain) {
                return $middleware->handle($req, $middlewareChain);
            };
```

Some sample code:

```php

use Attribute;
use App\Middlewares\CacheMiddleware;

/**
 * @Cache

 *
 * 示例：
 * #[Cache] // 默认缓存 60秒
 * #[Cache(ttl: 300)] // 缓存 5分钟
 * #[Cache(ttl: 600, key: 'home_page_data')] // 自定义 Key
 */
#[Attribute(Attribute::TARGET_CLASS | Attribute::TARGET_METHOD)]
class Cache implements MiddlewareProviderInterface
{
    /**
     * @param int         $ttl  缓存有效期（秒），默认 60 秒
     * @param string|null $key  自定义缓存 Key，留空则根据 URL 自动生成
     */
    public function __construct(
        public int $ttl = 60,
        public ?string $key = null
    ) {}

    public function getMiddleware(): string|array
    {
        return CacheMiddleware::class;
    }
}
```

